                <pb facs="0915" n="904" xml:id="pg904"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/845a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Zurich</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-11T16:00:00-04:00">August 11, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department would appreciate any information which you can discreetly obtain,
                    without consulting American delegates, as to position such delegates have taken
                    in World Zionist Congress on question of authorizing Zionist Executive to
                    negotiate with British Government <hi rendition="#italic">ad referendum</hi> on
                    Palestine partition scheme.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
